    "explanation": "Decision on trip TRP-02742. The disputed charge is the SGD 4.50 cancellation fee shown on EV-FARE-02742, which is CHARGED with no refund issued.\n\nThe driver's no-show fee stands. Under POL-NS-01 the fee is chargeable only if four things hold, and each does: (a) EV-TRIP-02742 records the driver's 'I'm Here' arrival event at 18:35:49; (b) EV-GPS-02742 places the driver inside the 50 m STANDARD-zone pickup geofence at that same time, and he had been stationary there from the first qualifying in-geofence fix at 18:35:49; (c) he held position continuously from that fix to the cancellation at 18:38:50 — 181 seconds against the 180-second free waiting period in force for this trip (platform_policy.free_wait_sec), measured from the first qualifying in-geofence fix and not from the arrival tap, as limb (c) requires; and (d) the trip was terminated by the driver at 18:38:50 with reason code RIDER_NO_SHOW, which limb (d) recognises, with no boarding event.\n\nThe rider's two shortfall arguments are rejected on the arithmetic. Both read the 181-second dwell as shorter than the 180-second minimum; 181 exceeds 180, so POL-NS-06's full-refund route is not engaged. The derived shortfall is -1.0 seconds — a one-second surplus, not a shortfall.\n\nPOL-NS-05 (false arrival marker) is not engaged: at the arrival timestamp the driver was 0.31 m from the pickup pin and stationary at 0 km/h, far inside the 300 m and 15 km/h triggers, so the waiting clock runs from the arrival event as recorded. POL-NS-03 (wrong entrance) is not engaged: the driver's stationary fixes lie inside the arrival radius, not outside it. POL-NS-04 (rider contact unanswered) is not engaged: the only message in EV-CHAT-02742 was sent by the driver, not the rider, so limb (a) fails; and the rider's own track in EV-GPS-02742 places her device a mean 625.9 m from the pin with zero qualifying fixes inside the 100 m STANDARD rider-presence radius, so limb (c) is affirmatively failed as well. POL-NS-11 therefore does not apply here — the limb could be run, and it was.\n\nWith POL-NS-01 satisfied in full and no clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displacing it, POL-NS-07 fixes the driver's payout at 80% of the SGD 4.50 fee = SGD 3.60 (matching the money block's driver_compensation figure). The anti-farming check does not trip: driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d is 0 (below 4) and 0 divided by 131 completed trips is 0.0 (below 0.08), so compensation is not withheld. Per POL-GEN-03 the emitted ruling is DRIVER_COMPENSATION, and amount_sgd carries the same SGD 3.60 figure; the rider's own charge is left as it stands.\n\nPOL-NS-09 escalation does not apply: confidence is above the 0.70 floor, no two admissible artifacts contradict each other on arrival, dwell or rider presence, neither party's disputes_with_counterparty_90d reaches 2 (both 0), the anti-farming check does not trip, and rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d is 1 (below 3). No clause produces a referral.\n\nEvidence weight: the deciding facts are carried by EV-TRIP-02742, EV-GPS-02742 and EV-FARE-02742, all at weight_multiplier 1.0, so the confidence cap is 1.0. The traffic-advisory artifact EV-ADVIS-02742-01 is MISSING (weight 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT); it carries no deciding fact here, because only one in-geofence dwell interval exists and POL-NS-06(i) accumulation is not needed. Two claims that cited that artifact without disclosing its impairment were discarded for that reason and are listed in the discarded-claims record. The monetary effect of SGD 3.60 does not exceed the SGD 8.00 execution threshold, so the ruling executes automatically."
