    "explanation": "To both parties. The rider's claim that the driver 'cancelled almost immediately' is not supported: the driver waited out the full free waiting period, so the SGD 4.50 cancellation fee stands and the driver is paid SGD 3.60 by the platform.\n\nWhat the record shows. Driver DRV-09742 accepted the trip at 18:29:40, tapped 'I'm Here' at 18:35:49, and the platform started the 180-second free waiting period in force for this STANDARD-zone trip (EV-TRIP-02742, platform_policy.free_wait_sec = 180). The GPS trace (EV-GPS-02742) places the driver inside the 50 m pickup radius from 18:35:49, with 19 qualifying fixes and held stationary there - minimum distance 0.31 m, speed 0 km/h - continuously until the driver cancelled at 18:38:50 with reason code RIDER_NO_SHOW, with no boarding event recorded.\n\nThe dwell question. POL-NS-01(c) measures the dwell from the first qualifying in-geofence GPS fix, not from the arrival tap and not from the wait-timer start at 18:35:51. That gives a continuous dwell of 181 seconds (18:35:49 to 18:38:50), which meets the 180-second minimum; the derived shortfall is -1.0 s, i.e. a surplus of one second. The rider's claims that the dwell runs 'only 181 seconds' and is 'one second short', and that POL-NS-06 therefore requires a full refund, are rejected on the arithmetic: 181 is greater than 180, not less, and the shortfall figure is negative, meaning the minimum was exceeded. POL-NS-06 is not engaged. All four limbs of POL-NS-01 hold: (a) a driver 'arrived' event exists; (b) the GPS places him inside the geofence at that timestamp; (c) the dwell of 181 seconds meets the free period; and (d) the trip was terminated by the driver with RIDER_NO_SHOW at or after the dwell elapsed. POL-NS-05 does not displace the clock (the arrival marker is true - he was stationary at the pickup point at 18:35:49), and POL-NS-03 does not apply because his stationary fixes lie inside the arrival radius, not in the 50-400 m wrong-entrance band. POL-NS-04 cannot exonerate the rider: she sent no locating message during the waiting window (the only message is the driver's, at 18:36:09), and her device sits a mean 625.9 m from the pin with zero qualifying fixes inside the 100 m radius, so limb (c) fails as well as limb (a).\n\nDriver compensation. Under POL-NS-07 the driver is paid 80 percent of the net fee of SGD 4.50, being SGD 3.60 (EV-FARE-02742 derived driver_compensation = 3.60). The anti-farming check does not trip - driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d is 0 and 0 divided by 131 completed trips is 0.0 - so compensation is paid, not withheld. Because compensation is paid, the ruling value is DRIVER_COMPENSATION and amount_sgd mirrors driver_compensation_sgd at SGD 3.60; the rider's charge of SGD 4.50 itself stands.\n\nEvidence integrity and weight. The fare ledger reconciles to the platform-policy figure of SGD 4.50, so no POL-NS-08(d) defect arises, and the GPS trace is complete (100 percent coverage, 10 s cadence, no gaps, both tracks present) with no POL-NS-08(a) or (b) impairment. EV-ADVIS-02742-01 is MISSING at weight 0.0, but no deciding fact rests on it - it bears only on POL-NS-06(i), which is not reached because the driver held a single continuous in-geofence run - so its absence does not cap confidence. The two claims citing that artifact were discarded because they did not disclose its issue code (MISSING_ARTIFACT), as POL-GEN-02(1) requires. The deciding facts (arrival and dwell) rest on EV-GPS-02742 and EV-TRIP-02742, each at weight 1.0, so the POL-GEN-02(2) cap is 1.0 and confidence is set at 0.90, above the 0.70 floor.\n\nNo escalation trigger under POL-NS-09 applies (confidence is above the floor; the artifacts do not contradict each other on arrival, dwell or rider presence; disputes_with_counterparty_90d is 0 on both sides; the anti-farming check does not trip and rider.no_show_disputes_30d is 1, below 3), and no clause produces a referral. The monetary effect is SGD 3.60, below the SGD 8.00 automatic-execution threshold, so the ruling is executed on issue. Either party may appeal under POL-GEN-04."
